Rāma hails Hanumān above Vālin Rāvaṇa --- Rāma lists leap Laṅkā burning Sītā comfort victory --- Rāma asks why Vālin spared amid Sugrīva feud --- Agastya blames sage curse hiding own strength --- Hungry Vāyu son leaps mistaking rising sun fruit --- Vāyu cools and sun spares approaching baby --- Rāhu complains to Indra of rival sun seizer --- Hanumān chases Rāhu then Airāvata as fruit --- Indra breaks jaw and Vāyu halts worlds breath --- Breathless gods seek Brahmā who leads them to Vāyu